{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80b4810a2c093682","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9017-E001\n3\ttitle: Keyboard accessibility fixes for the four audited Dashboard flows\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9017\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 8\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Keyboard accessibility fixes for the four audited Dashboard flows\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers full keyboard operability for the four audited core Dashboard flows — project creation, workbench spawn, model deployment, and pipeline run submission — by remediating the defects enumerated in the accessibility audit report: focus lost in modals, controls unreachable via keyboard, and inconsistent visible focus indicators. On completion, each of the four flows can be completed end-to-end with keyboard alone, with no focus traps, no unreachable controls, and a consistent focus-indicator treatment across the audited surfaces.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Remediate every keyboard-operability defect the audit report enumerates for the four audited flows:\n38\t  - **Project creation flow**\n39\t  - **Workbench spawn flow**\n40\t  - **Model deployment flow**\n41\t  - **Pipeline run submission flow**\n42\t- Fix focus management in modals so focus is trapped within open modals while they are open, restored to the invoking control on close, and never lost during open/close transitions.\n43\t- Make every control in the audited flows reachable and operable by keyboard alone (tab order, arrow-key navigation where the component pattern requires it, keyboard-activatable actions).\n44\t- Apply a consistent visible focus-indicator treatment across all interactive elements in the audited flows.\n45\t- Add keyboard-interaction test coverage for the remediated flows (focus trap behavior, tab reachability, focus-indicator presence) so the fixes are verifiable and regressions are caught.\n46\t- Incidental documentation touch-ups that fall out of these changes (e.g., updated screenshots or captions in existing docs where a fixed focus indicator appears) are folded in here as scope, not authored as new content.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Given the project creation flow, when a user completes it using keyboard input only, then every step is operable with no focus traps and no unreachable controls.\n51\t- Given the workbench spawn flow, when a user completes it using keyboard input only, then every step is operable with no focus traps and no unreachable controls.\n52\t- Given the model deployment flow, when a user completes it using keyboard input only, then every step is operable with no focus traps and no unreachable controls.\n53\t- Given the pipeline run submission flow, when a user completes it using keyboard input only, then every step is operable with no focus traps and no unreachable controls.\n54\t- Given any modal in the audited flows, when it opens, then focus moves into the modal and remains trapped within it until it closes, and on close focus returns to the control that invoked it.\n55\t- Given any interactive control in the audited flows, when it receives keyboard focus, then a visible focus indicator is rendered consistently with the indicator treatment used across all audited flows.\n56\t- Every defect item enumerated in the audit report for the four audited flows is addressed or explicitly dispositioned in the epic's tracking with rationale.\n57\t- Automated keyboard-interaction tests covering the four remediated flows pass in the component's CI.\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- **HLR-1 (P1)**: The four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard, with no focus traps or unreachable controls — this epic's core deliverable.\n62\t- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited flows — bundled into this epic because it is the same remediation sweep over the same flows and UI surfaces; a separate epic would re-traverse every touched component and force a second review pass.\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8bd53d610ad297ba","agent_id":"a253a8b96d51ddd1d","session_id":"eda13005-d007-48b0-bec9-257ea8435cf6","uuid":"035f7e92-1e60-4cd1-beb9-9fce5b0a580c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:14:41.079Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-80b4810a2c093682","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
