d — moving the affected success criteria to their corrected support levels based on the implemented state, including the focus-management and focus-indicator remediations.\n42\t- **Accessibility statement update**: revise the product docs accessibility statement so it accurately describes current keyboard accessibility support and any remaining known limitations that are out of scope for this strategy (e.g., screen-reader semantics beyond what the keyboard fixes require, flows outside the four audited ones).\n43\t- **Republication**: republish both documents through the standard documentation publishing process so the public conformance statement reflects the fixed state.\n44\t- **Technical review**: route the revised content through technical review against the implemented behavior before publication (see Acceptance Criteria).\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- The VPAT reflects the implemented keyboard-accessibility state of the four audited flows, with each affected success criterion stated at the support level that matches the shipped behavior.\n49\t- The product docs accessibility statement accurately describes the current keyboard accessibility support and explicitly lists remaining out-of-scope limitations.\n50\t- The revised documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented behavior (review sign-off recorded), confirming no claim in the conformance statement overstates or understates the shipped state.\n51\t- The updated VPAT and accessibility statement are republished and publicly available at their product documentation locations.\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- **HLR-3 (P2)**: The accessibility conformance documentation (VPAT and product docs accessibility statement) is updated and republished to reflect the fixed state, with technical review — this epic's entire deliverable.\n56\t\n57\t## Risks / Notes\n58\t\n59\t- Publication channels and review cadence for externally visible conformance statements may involve process timing outside the documentation team's direct control; the epic's engineering deliverable is the reviewed, submission-ready content and its republication through the standard process.\n60\t- The conformance claims must not be finalized until the Dashboard keyboard fixes are complete — the technical review gate exists to catch any drift between claimed and shipped state.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8bd53d610ad297ba","agent_id":"a253a8b96d51ddd1d","session_id":"eda13005-d007-48b0-bec9-257ea8435cf6","uuid":"94f2652c-4264-4e3a-a7cf-ad258d8dcd54","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:14:41.706Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e281a9086a70e60","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
